id=a52sxq_battery_info_regulatory
name=Galaxy A52s 5G: full Battery information page (cycle count, manufacture and first-use dates)
author=kusti420
description=Settings > About phone > Battery information only listed status, level and capacity. The other rows (battery_health_state, battery_cycle, battery_manufacture_date, battery_first_date; BatteryRegulatoryPreferenceController subclasses) are gated by BatteryInfoUtils.isAvailableBatteryRegulatory(), which needs BatteryManager.semGetValueAsBoolean(SEM_BATTERY_PROPERTY_IC_AUTHENTICATION_RESULT=106) == true, i.e. BattInfoManager (services.jar) having authenticated a Samsung battery auth IC through /sys/class/power_supply/sec_auth*/ or sbp-fg*/. The A52s has no such power supply, so BattInfoManager runs as mBatteryType 0 with IcAuthenticationResults [false] (dumpsys battery) and the rows are UNSUPPORTED. The data itself is there: /efs/FactoryApp/batt_discharge_level (cycles x100, maintained by the same BattInfoManager from /sys/class/power_supply/battery/battery_cycle), /efs/FactoryApp/HwParamBattQR (manufacture date) and /efs/FactoryApp/batt_beginning_date (first use). Samsung's own escape hatch for devices without the IC, SEC_FLOATING_FEATURE_SETTINGS_ENABLE_EU_BATTERY_REGULATORY_WITHOUT_IC, is additionally limited to KR models (Rune.isDomesticModel()); this sets that feature and drops the KR check, nothing else. Battery health stays "Unknown": it is SEM_BATTERY_PROPERTY_BSOH -> /efs/FactoryApp/bsoh, which only the auth-IC path writes (SohService's ANN estimate would land in bsoh0, which BatteryService never reads).
